-- writer-first.l4 with the sides of the RAND swapped. Before
-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1069 L4 ran the left side (possession) over the whole trace
-- first, so its read at 400 could not see the notice the right side records at
-- 10. The sides now take the trace's events in step, so the read sees the
-- notice and this file gives writer-first.l4's answer.

DECLARE Party IS ONE OF Landlord
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF `gives notice`, `seeks possession`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`notice` MEANS
    PARTY Landlord
    MAY `gives notice`
    WITHIN 100
    HENCE COMMIT `notice given` IS TRUE HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`possession` MEANS
    PARTY Landlord
    MAY `seeks possession` PROVIDED (RECALL OFFICIAL's `notice given`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    WITHIN 1000
    HENCE COMMIT `possession sought` IS TRUE HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`the tenancy` MEANS `possession` RAND `notice`

#TRACE `the tenancy` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Landlord DOES `gives notice` AT 10
    PARTY Landlord DOES `seeks possession` AT 400
